1. Bulbapedia wikitext — CC BY-NC-SA 2.5, NON-COMMERCIAL
--------------------------------------------------------

    tests/fixtures/wiki/*.json

Those files contain wikitext and parse trees recorded from Bulbapedia
(https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net) through this project's own throttled
client. They are here so the test suite can exercise the wiki parsers without
generating live traffic against a rate-limited wiki.

Bulbapedia content is licensed CC BY-NC-SA 2.5:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.5/

  * Attribution — Bulbapedia, and the page each fixture records. Each fixture
    carries its source page and revision id.
  * ShareAlike — adaptations must carry the same licence.
  * NonCommercial — you may not use this material commercially. This is the
    binding clause and it is not waivable by attribution.

`wiki_lookup` also fetches from Bulbapedia at runtime. Every response carries
`url` and `license` fields, so attribution travels with the content rather than
depending on a downstream consumer remembering it.

**If you build something commercial on this, the Bulbapedia tier has to be
dropped or replaced — not merely attributed.** See docs/DATA_SOURCES.md §1.


2. PokéAPI / veekun pokédex CSVs — permissive
----------------------------------------------

Ingested at build time from https://github.com/PokeAPI/pokeapi
(`data/v2/csv`), which derives from veekun's pokédex. Permissively licensed.
Not redistributed here — `poke-tools-build` downloads them, and the built
`data/pokedex.sqlite` is gitignored.


3. Pokémon Showdown learnsets — MIT
------------------------------------

Fetched at build time from https://play.pokemonshowdown.com/data/learnsets.json
(https://github.com/smogon/pokemon-showdown). Used as a cross-check against the
PokéAPI data, never as the primary source. Not redistributed here.
